    shocks, geopolitical events, and demand-side crises. Analysts should treat volatility as a first-order feature
    of oil markets and incorporate wide confidence intervals into any price forecast.
  </div>
</div>

</div><!-- /container -->

<div class="report-footer">
  <p>Data source: Global Fuel Price Trends (1970–2026) via Kaggle. All statistics computed directly from the dataset.
