    <li><strong>Iranian Revolution (1979):</strong> Prices rose from $14.50 in December 1978 to $40.75 in November 1979 (181% increase). Supply disruptions from the revolution and subsequent Iran-Iraq War kept prices elevated through the early 1980s.</li>
    <li><strong>1986 Oil Price Collapse:</strong> Prices crashed from $24.68 (Jan 1986) to $9.62 (Jul 1986) — a 61% decline in six months — as Saudi Arabia flooded the market. This marked the end of OPEC's effective price control.</li>
